      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #46037\n\nGLM tool-call parsers corrupt a bare JSON `null` inside `<arg_value>` when the tool schema is `anyOf: [{type: string}, {type: null}]` (or anything that makes `infer_type_from_json_schema` return `\\\"string\\\"`):\n\n- **glm4** (`Glm4MoeDetector`): `str(None)` → string `\\\"None\\\"`\n- **glm47** (`Glm47MoeDetector`): falls back to raw text → string `\\\"null\\\"`\n\n`json.loads(\\\"null\\\")` already yields Python `None`; the string coerce step then throws it away. Non-stream and stream/detect paths also disagree with each other.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `glm4_moe_detector.py`: keep `None` instead of `str(parsed_value)` in the string branch\n- `glm47_moe_detector.py`: keep `None` instead of raw `arg_value` when `parsed_value is None`\n- Regression tests for `anyOf[string, null]` on both detectors\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `TestGlm4MoeDetector.test_anyof_string_null_preserves_json_null`\n- [x] Unit: `test_glm47_schema_types` case `anyOf[{string},{null}] → None`\n- [ ] Optional: hit `/v1/chat/completions` with a GLM tool-call that emits `<arg_value>null</arg_value>` and confirm arguments stay JSON null\n\n## Related\n\n- Opposite-direction coercion: #43017\n- Same preserve-null principle as #42992\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40049504950](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40049504950)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40049504846](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40049504846)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40049504904](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40049504904)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
